   "source": [
    "# jpabm on Colab: reproduce the IPSS validation and run a scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells in order. About 2–4 minutes on the free CPU runtime. The first cell downloads the model from GitHub and installs it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "739a7ccb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
   　"import importlib.util, subprocess, sys, os\n",
   　"REPO = 'https://github.com/miraemog/jpabm.git'\n",
     "if not os.path.isdir('jpabm_repo'):\n",
     "    subprocess.check_call(['git', 'clone', '-q', REPO, 'jpabm_repo'])\n",
     "if importlib.util.find_spec('jpabm') is None:\n",
     "    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '-q', '-e', './jpabm_repo'])\n",
     "import jpabm; print('jpabm', jpabm.__version__)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0fe2e6c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Validation table (model vs IPSS 2023, fertility- and mortality-medium)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7c593cd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from jpabm.validate import validate, summarize, pension_check\n",
    "rows, R = validate(n_runs=12, n_agents=100_000)\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index('year')[['pop_model','pop_ipss','dep_model','dep_ipss','old_model','old_ipss','work_model','work_ipss','kid_model','kid_ipss']].round(1)\n",
    "display(df); print(summarize(rows)); print(pension_check(R))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62caa165",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Policy scenarios on equal footing (+100k people/year)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "17c098e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from jpabm import Params, run_many, data as D\n",
    "N = 60_000\n",
    "sc = {'baseline': Params(n_agents=N),\n",
    "      'immigration +100k/yr': Params(n_agents=N, net_immigration=D.IPSS_FOREIGN_NET_INFLOW + 100_000),\n",
    "      'births +100k/yr (TFR +0.18)': Params(n_agents=N, tfr_delta=0.18),\n",
    "      'retirement age 68': Params(n_agents=N, retirement_age=68)}\n",
    "res = {k: run_many(p, 10, 2000) for k, p in sc.items()}\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
    "yrs = res['baseline']['year']\n",
    "for k, r in res.items():\n",
    "    ax[0].plot(yrs, np.nanmean(r['pop'], 0)/1e6, label=k); ax[1].plot(yrs, np.nanmean(r['dependency'], 0)); ax[2].plot(yrs, np.nanmean(r['replacement'], 0))\n",
    "ax[0].plot(D.YEARS, [D.IPSS_POP_K[y]/1e3 for y in D.YEARS], 'k--', label='IPSS')\n",
    "ax[1].plot(D.YEARS, [D.IPSS_DEPENDENCY[y] for y in D.YEARS], 'k--')\n",
    "for a, t in zip(ax, ['Population (M)', 'Dependency index', 'Pension pressure index (%)']): a.set_title(t)\n",
    "ax[0].legend(fontsize=8); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Economy and public finances (new in v0.2)\n",
    "The same model now carries a fiscal block: real GDP from labour input and productivity, social security by age structure, the pension replacement rate with the macro-economic slide (floor 50%), the national primary balance, ordinary government bonds, and interest payments. Scope is the national general account only. Growth does not depend on tax, interest rates or inflation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
    "from jpabm import Params, run_many, data as D\n",
    "N, R = 60_000, 10\n",
    "F = D.IPSS_FOREIGN_NET_INFLOW\n",
    "sc = {'baseline': Params(n_agents=N),\n",
    "      'immigration +100k/yr': Params(n_agents=N, net_immigration=F+100_000),\n",
    "      'pension age 68': Params(n_agents=N, retirement_age=68),\n",
    "      'consumption tax 15%': Params(n_agents=N, tax_consumption=15),\n",
    "      'long-term yield 4%': Params(n_agents=N, long_yield=4.0),\n",
    "      'inflation 3%, yield 2.5%': Params(n_agents=N, inflation=3.0),\n",
    "      'inflation 3%, yield 3.5%': Params(n_agents=N, inflation=3.0, long_yield=3.5),\n",
    "      'productivity 1.5%': Params(n_agents=N, productivity=1.5)}\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "for k, p in sc.items():\n",
    "    r = run_many(p, R, 100); m = lambda key, i: float(np.nanmean(r[key][:, i]))\n",
    "    rows.append(dict(scenario=k, real_gdp_2070=m('f_real', 50), debt_pct_gdp_2070=m('f_debtgdp', 50),\n",
    "                     interest_over_tax_2050=m('f_inttax', 30), primary_balance_2050=m('f_pb', 30), replacement_2060=m('replacement', 40)))\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index('scenario').round(1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Check the web simulator against this model\n",
